# openclaw is DELIBERATELY NOT in this list (removed 2026-08-27).
#
# ceres runs the beta channel (~/.openclaw/openclaw.json `update.channel:
# "beta"`). `openclaw@latest` here was the root cause of four silent
# beta->stable downgrades (2026-08-17 x2, 2026-08-22 16:26, 2026-08-26 02:02
# +1000): the stable binary refuses a beta-written config, exits 78 with
# `InvalidConfigError: ... meta: Invalid input`, bricking every CLI call and
# the gateway on its next restart. Each downgrade landed 2-3 min after a
# fast-forward `git pull` here -- the pull fires scripts/post-merge, which runs
# deploy.zsh, whose scripts/deploy.d/70_runtime_installs.zsh:74 does
# `mise exec node -- npm install -g $npm_packages` over this list.
#
# Pinning to @beta fixed the version skew but not the deeper hazard: any deploy
# reinstalls openclaw *under the live gateway*, rewriting dist/ beneath a
# running process and breaking its lazy module loading until restart (see the
# 2026-08-24T14:54 SIGTERM-mid-postinstall entry in
# ~/.cache/openclaw-ensure-beta.log). So the package is out of the sweep
# entirely and ownership moved to two places that cannot fire mid-run:
#   - upgrades: openclaw's own in-gateway beta auto-updater
#   - repair/install: ~/repos/hart/scripts/openclaw-ensure-beta.sh, the
#     ExecStartPre guard on openclaw-gateway.service (handles a missing package
#     too, so a node bump self-heals on the next gateway start)
# Full evidence chain: ~/repos/hart/docs/openclaw-beta-drift-check.md
# tsc/tsserver + the LSP server nvim's ts_ls uses.
